# Example film script for Scene Builder.
# Script window → Build Film. Edit anything and build again.

REQUIRES: Scene Builder 1.5
TITLE: The Promise
LOCATION: Lakeside Campfire
TIME: 18.0 -> 19.0
WEATHER: mist 0.3, wind 0.25
MUSIC: theme, volume -5

CAST:
Mira = woman casual, top teal, bottom navy, hair ponytail, height 1.64
Grandpa = elder, top brown, bottom grey

SET:
lamp = torch right of bench

SCENE 1: The way home
Grandpa sits on bench
Mira is at hill
SHOT: establishing, crane down
TITLE: THE PROMISE for 4s
WAIT 4s
SHOT: follow Mira
Mira walks to clearing via path
SHOT: medium on Grandpa, from left, dolly in
Grandpa looks at Mira
Grandpa: "I knew you would come back before dark."

# No SHOT lines here: Scene Builder films this scene by itself.
SCENE 2: By the fire
Mira walks to campfire
Mira (to Grandpa): "I promised, didn't I?"
Grandpa nods
Grandpa: "Your grandmother made the same promise, sixty years ago."
Mira (to Grandpa): "Did she keep it?"
WAIT 1s
Grandpa: "Every single evening. Right here."
Mira sits on bench 1

SCENE 3: Night falls
TIME: 19.6 over 6s
LIGHT: mist 0.55 over 6s
SHOT: two-shot Mira and Grandpa, static
Grandpa (raises hand): "Look. The first star."
SHOT: close-up on Mira, from right
Mira looks at lake
WAIT 2s
SHOT: aerial, orbit left
WAIT 5s
TITLE: THE END for 4s
WAIT 4s
